{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/898016-moodsetting-a-long-running-chronicle","id":898016,"title":"Moodsetting a long-running chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T11:21:24-07:00","id":898016,"title":"Moodsetting a long-running chronicle","content":"There's an experiment that I'd like to urge other storytellers to try. Most of us spend a lot of time piecing together a soundtrack to go with our chronicles. There's always one song that really fits, but it's not like you can put it on a loop for the whole game. Instead, what if you choose that one song, almost like an intro theme for a TV series, and play it every time during the previous session's recap.<br /> <br /> It's non-invasive and I find it instantly grounds the players in the story's mood. Let me know your results if you try it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T00:34:03-07:00","id":901845,"title":"","content":"I haven't tried it per say, but I have attached certain themes to certain games I play with a friend which were the first theme played when we started it; so I do think there is some effect of what you describe. Usually though, whether as a ST or a player, I either don't use any music or I put something on myself according to my mood; but I'm gonna give it a go to play a specific theme according to a specific session ahead and see how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:08:53-07:00","id":923543,"title":"","content":"I haven't taken long at all with the reply!<br /> Anyway from what I can tell so far there are no obvious hints of any themes getting stuck to my player so all I can bring is an anecdotal that for me I have a few themes in my head I automatically related to where I heard them from, namely certain sessions that were memorable to me.Maybe just do it and see what happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:49:05-07:00","id":923645,"title":"","content":"I used to play the Interview with a Vampire soundtrack during games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&am